WEBVTT

00:02.290 --> 00:04.729
Do you know about the Big Ol' Moa?

00:04.730 --> 00:06.959
It looks similar to Mr. Ostrich.

00:06.960 --> 00:08.589
Wow!

00:08.590 --> 00:12.909
Mr. Dodo is popular among
the extinct animals, huh?

00:12.910 --> 00:14.959
There are some that are
similar to kitty cats too.

00:14.960 --> 00:17.889
Wow! You're very
knowledgeable, Sengoku-kun.

00:17.890 --> 00:19.020
What should I do?

00:19.370 --> 00:22.770
I'm so curious about how he names
them that I can't focus on this story.

00:24.010 --> 00:27.759
Hori-san and Miyamura-kun
is about to start!

00:27.760 --> 00:31.259
Man, was it a doggy
rather than a kitty cat?

00:29.756 --> 00:36.390
LIVE-EVIL FANSUBS Presents

00:31.260 --> 00:34.540
Sengoku-san, isn't it
too late to be saying that?

00:35.060 --> 00:36.060
Huh?

00:42.810 --> 00:44.990
Man, it's hot.

00:46.770 --> 00:47.770
Whoa, it's hot!

00:48.350 --> 00:49.570
It's stifling!

00:50.630 --> 00:51.990
Hori-san...

00:52.400 --> 00:54.179
What are you doing?

00:54.180 --> 00:56.490
I'm waiting for Ishikawa-kun.

00:58.420 --> 01:00.969
You're waiting here?
You should wait for him in the classroom.

01:00.970 --> 01:02.700
It's because they've started cleaning up.

01:03.720 --> 01:05.650
You're hopeless.

01:06.840 --> 01:08.210
Here, have some ice cream.

01:08.850 --> 01:10.550
Why don't you eat it with Tooru?

01:10.940 --> 01:12.039
Are you sure?

01:12.040 --> 01:13.609
Oh, how much do I owe you?

01:13.610 --> 01:15.970
Don't sweat it. It was half-priced.

01:16.740 --> 01:19.850
I felt bad, since you always
bring me cakes and stuff.

01:20.590 --> 01:21.829
Thank you.

01:21.830 --> 01:22.830
Yep.

01:23.170 --> 01:25.370
You should wait for him in the shade.

01:31.130 --> 01:32.480
I see.

01:32.810 --> 01:34.739
Hori gave you these?

01:34.740 --> 01:35.990
Hori did, huh?

01:39.240 --> 01:41.459
I can't eat the melon-flavored ones!

01:41.460 --> 01:43.199
Sorry, I didn't know.

01:43.200 --> 01:45.619
No, it's not your fault, Miyamura.

01:45.620 --> 01:46.849
It's because I... I...

01:46.850 --> 01:48.250
I'm really sorry.

01:48.870 --> 01:50.519
You can have this if you want.

01:50.520 --> 01:53.250
Whoa! Thanks for real!

01:54.240 --> 01:56.260
It's hot!

01:56.570 --> 01:57.940
- Sen-chan!
- Student council president!

01:57.941 --> 01:58.550
Huh?

01:58.880 --> 02:01.149
Low-energy vanilla or...

02:01.150 --> 02:03.479
Energetic, but despised melon!

02:03.480 --> 02:04.560
- Which is better?!
- Which is better?!

02:05.270 --> 02:06.270
What?

02:06.510 --> 02:08.060
What are you talking about?

02:11.230 --> 02:12.600
Pretty plain.

02:12.960 --> 02:14.490
What a relief.

02:14.960 --> 02:17.000
Am I the only one who's not cooling off?

02:17.440 --> 02:19.579
I won! It says I won!

02:19.580 --> 02:20.749
Even though it's a cup?

02:20.750 --> 02:22.520
That's amazing, President!

02:23.040 --> 02:25.639
Ishikawa-kun, feel free to
redeem it for another one.

02:25.640 --> 02:27.189
Even though I'm a high-school senior?

02:27.190 --> 02:28.789
Wouldn't that be embarrassing?

02:28.790 --> 02:31.209
All you have to say is,
"May I please have one?"

02:31.210 --> 02:32.210
Like hell I could.

02:32.570 --> 02:34.140
Rock! Paper! Scissors!

02:35.850 --> 02:37.850
Miyamura, I'll have strawberry.

02:38.380 --> 02:40.160
Come on! Strawberry, please!

02:40.870 --> 02:43.139
Shut up!

02:43.140 --> 02:45.100
He doesn't have to run.

02:45.500 --> 02:49.329
Sengoku, is the student
council room always open?

02:49.330 --> 02:50.330
Why?

02:51.410 --> 02:54.370
I was just there and it
was really cool in there.

02:55.800 --> 02:57.439
Let me chill there next time.

02:57.440 --> 03:00.660
Go to the nurse's office
if you need to cool off.

03:02.520 --> 03:05.450
Bamboo, bamboo, shoot shoot shoot.

03:12.050 --> 03:13.539
O-One shoot!

03:13.540 --> 03:14.739
Two shoots!

03:14.740 --> 03:15.740
Three shoots!

03:15.880 --> 03:17.099
Four shoots!

03:17.100 --> 03:18.120
Wha?!

03:21.170 --> 03:23.169
You both lose.

03:23.170 --> 03:26.009
I don't want to hear it from someone
who didn't say "shoot" at the end.

03:26.010 --> 03:28.520
Hori and Miyamura, you both
have to endure the penalty, OK?

03:30.120 --> 03:31.739
I'll have an orange juice.

03:31.740 --> 03:33.440
Strawberry milk.

03:36.240 --> 03:38.560
Always cheating out of saying "shoot"!

03:38.810 --> 03:40.900
Huh? Did you say something?

03:41.680 --> 03:45.950
Hey, are you sure Hori-san and
Miyamura-kun aren't an item?

03:46.960 --> 03:48.339
Who knows?

03:48.340 --> 03:49.340
Oh...

03:49.850 --> 03:55.039
But if you ask me, Hori-san would be
a better match with Ishikawa-kun.

03:55.040 --> 03:56.879
Huh? R-Really?

03:56.880 --> 03:57.960
Geez...

03:58.500 --> 04:01.259
Give up on Hori already.

04:01.260 --> 04:03.260
N-No way!

04:05.670 --> 04:08.299
You'd have to be a complete
masochist, you know...

04:08.300 --> 04:10.570
Oh! What? What are you talking about?

04:13.690 --> 04:15.429
Oh, whose was that again?

04:15.430 --> 04:16.730
Ishikawa-kun's.

04:17.870 --> 04:18.920
It's Tooru's...

04:19.230 --> 04:22.740
Ah! Wh-What the hell?! What should I do?

04:23.240 --> 04:25.960
Wait a second, it actually might be the
student council president's.

04:26.980 --> 04:28.029
Sengoku's, huh?

04:28.030 --> 04:31.910
What the hell's going on? Such a waste!

04:32.720 --> 04:34.280
Either way...

04:34.770 --> 04:36.040
It should be funny.

04:38.350 --> 04:40.650
They're taking their
sweet time getting our stuff.

04:41.900 --> 04:43.470
They're probably doing something.

04:45.200 --> 04:46.200
Oh!

04:46.810 --> 04:49.419
I didn't mean it in a bad way. Um...

04:49.420 --> 04:50.519
That's right.

04:50.520 --> 04:54.140
What do you think they would do on
campus during the middle of the day?

04:54.800 --> 04:57.480
That's exactly why they're
probably doing something...

05:00.640 --> 05:01.649
Geez!

05:01.650 --> 05:03.589
It's because you weren't paying attention!

05:03.590 --> 05:04.670
Sorry.

05:05.500 --> 05:08.219
It's because you said
something weird, Sakura.

05:08.220 --> 05:09.910
I said the wrong thing.

05:11.740 --> 05:14.670
Hey, Tooru, don't worry about it.

05:14.670 --> 05:18.509
I bet it's because Miyamura
dropped the change or something.

05:15.120 --> 05:18.040
Esper

05:18.510 --> 05:21.629
Your kindness is heartwarming, Yoshikawa.

05:21.630 --> 05:23.209
I'm gonna write that in today's log.

05:23.210 --> 05:25.210
That's not the place to
write something like that.

05:25.820 --> 05:27.510
Don't mess up my hair!

05:28.450 --> 05:29.610
Mess up...

05:31.720 --> 05:33.179
Thanks for waiting.

05:33.180 --> 05:34.889
Sorry for being late.

05:34.890 --> 05:36.359
Welcome back!

05:36.360 --> 05:37.450
Here's your orange juice.

05:38.050 --> 05:39.889
Strawberry milk.

05:39.890 --> 05:40.890
Yay!

05:41.200 --> 05:43.579
Ishikawa-kun? Ishikawa-kun?

05:43.580 --> 05:44.580
Huh?

05:44.780 --> 05:47.389
Sorry, I "did it".

05:47.390 --> 05:49.179
D-Did what?

05:49.180 --> 05:55.539
Um, you see, when we went to buy juice just
now... I feel really bad about it, Ishikawa-kun.

05:55.540 --> 05:56.799
I need to apologize to y-

05:56.800 --> 05:58.940
Stop, I don't want to hear it! Stop!

06:00.820 --> 06:02.940
- Huh? What's wrong?
- I can't hear you! I can't hear you!

06:02.943 --> 06:04.740
Actually, you see...

06:05.840 --> 06:06.970
What?!

06:07.710 --> 06:09.349
That's bad, you know.

06:09.350 --> 06:12.820
Yeah, if it were me, I would get
really mad at the person who did that.

06:13.200 --> 06:15.240
That's what I'd expect
from you, Sengoku-kun!

06:15.980 --> 06:16.980
Yoshikawa...

06:17.660 --> 06:19.829
You have a box cutter, right?

06:19.830 --> 06:21.509
Can you stab me right round here?

06:22.610 --> 06:27.069
Ishikawa-kun, you see,
it was... um... because...

06:27.070 --> 06:28.949
I was careless.

06:28.950 --> 06:31.919
You're right. That was careless.

06:31.920 --> 06:33.030
Very careless.

06:33.460 --> 06:34.879
They said it was carelessness.

06:34.880 --> 06:36.199
Well, don't worry about it.

06:36.200 --> 06:37.620
"Don't worry about it" my ass!

06:38.000 --> 06:40.500
Oh, come on. Does it
really matter if it's a cola?

06:40.940 --> 06:41.940
A cola?

06:42.770 --> 06:43.919
Wh-What the hell?!

06:43.920 --> 06:45.919
Hey! Wait, Miyamura!

06:45.920 --> 06:47.359
I said I'm sorry!

06:47.360 --> 06:48.230
Ah, the floor!

06:48.230 --> 06:49.889
Oh, man.

06:48.231 --> 06:49.890
- The floor!
- Now, now...

06:49.890 --> 06:51.270
Ishikawa-kun...

06:49.890 --> 06:52.790
Anyway, please calm down, everyone.

06:50.840 --> 06:52.789
You're so clumsy!

06:52.790 --> 06:54.100
Cola shoe!

06:52.790 --> 06:54.099
It's spilling... Ah!

06:54.100 --> 06:55.100
Are you OK?

07:01.350 --> 07:04.650
The student council president
just called you "Kyou-chan".

07:05.460 --> 07:08.370
Kyou-chan, do you have enough rags?

07:09.080 --> 07:13.010
Oh, everyone called
me that when I was a kid.

07:13.810 --> 07:14.810
What about you, Miyamura?

07:15.480 --> 07:17.500
Just Miyamura.

07:18.200 --> 07:20.240
Or "dark".

07:20.900 --> 07:21.580
Huh?

07:21.581 --> 07:23.829
Oh, r-really?

07:23.830 --> 07:25.589
Oh, great.

07:25.590 --> 07:30.130
Oh, but my parents call me "Ikkun".

07:30.850 --> 07:32.130
Ikkun!

07:32.500 --> 07:34.210
I'm telling everyone tomorrow.

07:34.930 --> 07:37.510
It's embarrassing, so
try not to call me that.

07:38.380 --> 07:39.180
Oh!

07:39.181 --> 07:41.140
I'm back.

07:42.110 --> 07:44.060
Welcome back! What's wrong?

07:44.780 --> 07:46.939
I just came back to
get a change of clothes.

07:46.940 --> 07:49.360
But I have to go back right away.

07:49.960 --> 07:51.270
I see.

07:51.740 --> 07:53.019
Good evening.

07:53.020 --> 07:54.069
Thank you for having me over.

07:54.070 --> 07:57.790
Oh, Izumi-kun! I saw the magazine article.

07:58.720 --> 07:59.720
Huh?

08:02.230 --> 08:05.010
So this is your house, Miyamura?

08:05.890 --> 08:06.320
Oh!

08:06.800 --> 08:07.800
Huh?!

08:09.180 --> 08:12.319
I thought they would only put my
dad, who was in front of me, on there.

08:12.320 --> 08:13.809
That's amazing!

08:13.810 --> 08:17.239
I'll brag about this to your dad, even
though I haven't seen him in two years.

08:17.240 --> 08:19.449
Why are you going to tell dad about it?

08:19.450 --> 08:21.739
He's like one of the
children in the family, right?

08:21.740 --> 08:24.829
I'll tell your father that
we have one more child.

08:24.830 --> 08:26.440
Geez! Don't do that!

08:31.560 --> 08:34.570
Izumi-kun, feel free to
come over any time, OK?

08:34.870 --> 08:38.580
OK. Well, I'll be going now.

08:51.550 --> 08:53.070
Oh, Miyamura-kun!

08:54.540 --> 08:57.180
Is this your family's store?

08:57.740 --> 08:58.740
Uh...

08:58.910 --> 08:59.470
Yeah.

08:59.471 --> 09:02.430
Oh, that's amazing! You're famous!

09:03.930 --> 09:08.230
Oh, that's unusual. Girls
are flocking all over Miyamura.

09:10.300 --> 09:12.199
My mechanical pencil broke.

09:12.200 --> 09:13.340
Let me borrow yours, Tooru.

09:13.750 --> 09:15.950
Usually, the lead is what breaks.

09:16.850 --> 09:19.450
Um, who's this guy?

09:20.740 --> 09:21.919
He's so cool!

09:21.920 --> 09:22.939
Yep!

09:22.940 --> 09:24.840
Hey, who is he?

09:26.530 --> 09:27.669
A part-timer.

09:27.670 --> 09:29.510
Wow...

09:28.130 --> 09:29.509
Oh, really?

09:29.510 --> 09:32.090
Crap, my ruler broke.

09:32.480 --> 09:33.670
You can have mine.

09:49.920 --> 09:52.149
Yuki, your hands are small.

09:52.150 --> 09:52.940
There!

09:52.941 --> 09:54.999
Uh... what?

09:55.000 --> 09:57.689
Doesn't your heart beat faster when
somebody suddenly grabs your hands?

09:57.690 --> 09:58.739
Really?

09:58.740 --> 10:00.119
Of course it does!

10:00.120 --> 10:01.159
Squeeze!

10:01.160 --> 10:02.809
Th-That hurts.

10:02.810 --> 10:03.730
Good morning.

10:03.730 --> 10:04.400
Good mor-

10:04.400 --> 10:05.400
Huh?

10:06.070 --> 10:07.670
What happened to your face?

10:08.090 --> 10:09.400
I got punched.

10:09.810 --> 10:11.379
I got into a little fight.

10:11.380 --> 10:13.019
That's awful!

10:13.020 --> 10:15.879
A fight? But they didn't need to punch you.

10:15.880 --> 10:17.630
Who did that to you?

10:17.880 --> 10:19.289
Ishikawa-kun.

10:19.290 --> 10:20.280
Tooru?

10:20.280 --> 10:21.280
Um...

10:22.020 --> 10:23.500
Oh, good morning.

10:25.040 --> 10:26.640
What's the reason?

10:28.840 --> 10:31.120
It's none of your business.

10:33.010 --> 10:34.270
Oh, it's only...

10:34.280 --> 10:37.460
a matter of time before
they find out this is you, Miyamura.

10:38.940 --> 10:41.589
Just let it go already.
Why not cut your hair?

10:41.590 --> 10:45.339
No way. I want to keep
living as a dull person.

10:45.340 --> 10:46.660
Oh?

10:47.350 --> 10:50.430
Hori-san will get mad,
so I don't want anyone to find out.

10:51.930 --> 10:55.389
Hey, what's really going on?

10:55.390 --> 10:56.390
Huh?

10:56.610 --> 10:58.670
Between you and Hori?

10:59.610 --> 11:01.579
That again?

11:01.580 --> 11:03.190
Don't tell me "that again".

11:04.330 --> 11:07.600
It's not like we're a couple or anything.

11:10.370 --> 11:13.630
Ishikawa-kun, do you still like Hori-san?

11:13.960 --> 11:15.530
What do you mean by "still"?

11:17.530 --> 11:20.450
I already know that I
don't have a chance in hell.

11:22.450 --> 11:25.059
Listen to me! Seriously!

11:25.060 --> 11:27.330
I am listening! Don't worry.

11:28.520 --> 11:30.310
Hori likes you.

11:31.330 --> 11:36.070
That's not true. It's
just your imagination.

11:36.470 --> 11:39.670
No, actually, it's true.

11:40.190 --> 11:41.230
Just kidding...

11:41.760 --> 11:42.980
This is psychological warfare.

11:43.900 --> 11:47.730
But what will you do if
Hori actually asks you that?

11:48.300 --> 11:50.420
Will you change the subject
the way you did just now?

11:50.950 --> 11:55.109
Hori-san only sees me as a friend.

11:55.110 --> 11:56.899
How can you be so sure?!

11:56.900 --> 11:58.030
Ishikawa-kun, you're also...

11:58.500 --> 11:59.500
I...

12:03.780 --> 12:06.279
It's because you startled me.

12:06.280 --> 12:09.010
You stubborn mule!

12:10.080 --> 12:12.979
Wh-What gives you the right to say that?!

12:12.980 --> 12:14.909
You won't get it unless I tell you!

12:14.910 --> 12:15.580
What do you mean?!

12:15.581 --> 12:17.230
Like I said, Hori...

12:21.950 --> 12:22.950
Sorry.

12:27.150 --> 12:29.330
Those are my eyes! My eyes! Stop it!

12:37.470 --> 12:38.190
Shut up.

12:38.191 --> 12:40.009
It's self-defense.

12:40.010 --> 12:41.890
But I'm all bruised and battered!

12:43.470 --> 12:46.700
I don't know how you're punching,

12:47.440 --> 12:49.390
but you don't feel any pain, do you?

12:53.700 --> 12:58.260
I'm sorry I pestered
you and raised my voice.

12:59.720 --> 13:02.720
You just got startled, right?

13:03.480 --> 13:05.969
No, I did get a bit mad.

13:05.970 --> 13:09.150
Don't be so honest about it!
It makes it that much more scary!

13:10.600 --> 13:13.139
Tooru said it was his fault.

13:13.140 --> 13:16.230
Miyamura said that <i>he</i>
was to blame for it all.

13:16.540 --> 13:18.979
They punch each other,
and yet they're looking out for each other.

13:18.980 --> 13:19.530
Weird!

13:19.850 --> 13:21.249
I know, right?

13:21.250 --> 13:24.150
Geez! Why did this happen?

13:28.110 --> 13:31.360
Guys are lucky, aren't they?
They can get into fights like that.

13:32.260 --> 13:33.750
For sure.

13:37.000 --> 13:40.000
A few years ago... At this school...

13:40.300 --> 13:43.510
strange phenomena sometimes occured.

13:43.511 --> 13:45.510
H-Hori-san, you don't like blueberries?

13:45.510 --> 13:48.510
No, I don't like how they're a bit sour.

13:45.850 --> 13:48.510
Those who were pursuing...

13:49.800 --> 13:53.399
What was it that they saw?

13:53.400 --> 13:54.400
Hey!

13:57.020 --> 14:00.010
S-Souta isn't home yet?

14:00.490 --> 14:03.319
He went off to play soccer at 7 AM too.

14:03.320 --> 14:04.749
I can't believe it.

14:04.750 --> 14:08.530
Ever since he got into elementary school,
he's been going out to play a lot, huh?

14:09.160 --> 14:11.070
Do you understand?

14:13.570 --> 14:14.570
Let's see...

14:15.390 --> 14:16.609
Which one do you want to watch next?

14:16.610 --> 14:18.540
How many volumes are there?

14:19.200 --> 14:19.870
Oh...

14:19.870 --> 14:20.620
Huh?

14:20.621 --> 14:23.000
You've got a cut on your hand.

14:24.280 --> 14:25.679
It's been there for a long time.

14:25.680 --> 14:27.369
Did you break the bone or something?

14:27.370 --> 14:29.110
Nope, I've had it since birth.

14:30.310 --> 14:32.379
Miyamura, your hands are pale.

14:32.380 --> 14:33.429
Really?

14:33.430 --> 14:36.279
And your fingers are
slender, like a woman's.

14:36.280 --> 14:37.460
Oh?

14:38.220 --> 14:41.229
How weird, your hand is bigger than mine.

14:41.230 --> 14:43.459
Huh? Isn't that normal?

14:43.460 --> 14:46.029
You see, I've got big hands.

14:46.030 --> 14:48.279
Oh, you have a callus
on your middle finger.

14:48.280 --> 14:49.280
What was that?

14:49.650 --> 14:51.560
It's the hands of a scholar.

15:08.750 --> 15:11.100
I l-love y...

15:13.860 --> 15:14.860
Huh?

15:14.970 --> 15:20.440
Your hands... I just think
your hands are nice, Miyamura.

15:20.810 --> 15:21.810
My hands?

15:21.960 --> 15:26.299
That's right. I was just
thinking that I... love them.

15:26.300 --> 15:29.369
I don't have calluses
like you do, Hori-san.

15:29.370 --> 15:31.390
Oh, shut up!

15:32.100 --> 15:33.390
I see.

15:33.970 --> 15:35.580
I love yours too.

15:36.440 --> 15:37.440
I see...

15:44.150 --> 15:45.180
I love you.

15:46.770 --> 15:48.330
I already heard that just now.

15:49.830 --> 15:50.830
Yeah.

15:59.010 --> 16:01.190
Well, I'll see you at school.

16:02.050 --> 16:03.050
OK.

16:12.820 --> 16:15.560
Was I acting normally?

16:21.350 --> 16:22.880
Miyamura!

16:24.290 --> 16:25.290
Shindou...

16:25.630 --> 16:27.090
Long time no see!

16:27.970 --> 16:30.509
I see you've got a lot
of ear piercings as usual.

16:30.510 --> 16:31.579
I guess.

16:31.580 --> 16:35.939
Huh? Did you get more? You didn't
have this many during junior high.

16:35.940 --> 16:36.940
Yeah.

16:37.570 --> 16:40.239
Anyway, I'm so jealous.

16:40.240 --> 16:40.700
Huh?

16:41.210 --> 16:42.420
Huh? Aren't you a senior?

16:42.420 --> 16:45.960
Ah! No, I'm not! Stop
saying stupid stuff like that!

16:42.421 --> 16:44.500
Continuing education

16:44.501 --> 16:46.610
Held back (Cigarettes)

16:46.320 --> 16:49.889
That's not what I meant.
You're usually walking with a girl, right?

16:49.890 --> 16:53.159
You seem a bit tough when your hair's down.

16:53.160 --> 16:54.639
Are you talking about Hori-san?

16:54.640 --> 16:56.129
Her name is Hori-san?

16:56.130 --> 16:58.119
Uh... yeah.

16:58.120 --> 17:01.189
That must be nice. I want a girlfriend too.

17:01.190 --> 17:03.489
S-She's not my girlfriend.

17:03.490 --> 17:04.999
You're lying.

17:05.000 --> 17:06.919
Everybody's saying that now.

17:06.920 --> 17:07.860
Everybody?

17:07.860 --> 17:08.540
Yeah.

17:08.541 --> 17:10.690
Like Iijima and Kanihara.

17:14.630 --> 17:18.270
Shugo... can... not... help...

17:18.620 --> 17:25.170
The "ing" ending for a verb means
"so and so" has to perform an action.

17:19.140 --> 17:22.640
I love you?

17:23.160 --> 17:25.170
Hori-san was joking...

17:25.170 --> 17:27.300
She's just teasing me.

17:25.210 --> 17:27.950
I'm going to have you all give it a try.

17:28.400 --> 17:31.900
- Give me an answer for when you have to perform an action.
- I love you?

17:28.400 --> 17:30.150
I was

17:28.560 --> 17:30.150
Definitely about your hands.

17:30.151 --> 17:31.900
talking about your hands.

17:30.151 --> 17:31.900
It was

17:32.310 --> 17:33.879
Complete this sentence, Hori.

17:33.880 --> 17:35.819
She's not here yet.

17:35.820 --> 17:37.659
Huh? Is she absent?

17:37.660 --> 17:41.660
I didn't mean it like that

17:38.380 --> 17:40.419
Well then, I pick you, Yoshikawa.

17:40.420 --> 17:41.660
Ah!

17:44.030 --> 17:46.980
Even Hori-san is absent
without permission sometimes, huh?

17:47.710 --> 17:48.849
Any word from her?

17:48.850 --> 17:50.590
I texted her just now.

17:51.590 --> 17:52.590
Miyamura!

17:56.030 --> 17:57.030
Are you OK?

17:58.510 --> 18:01.229
Hey, either try getting out of the way
or try catching it, will you!

18:01.230 --> 18:02.230
What about your glasses?

18:02.650 --> 18:05.029
They should be fine, I think.

18:05.030 --> 18:06.030
Your nose is bleeding!

18:07.270 --> 18:08.900
Stress?

18:09.140 --> 18:12.209
Yeah. You feel sick
and get agitated, right?

18:12.210 --> 18:14.139
I'm going to the staff room for a bit.

18:14.140 --> 18:15.900
What'll you do? Lie down?

18:16.740 --> 18:17.999
I'll sit here.

18:18.000 --> 18:19.000
I see.

18:27.540 --> 18:29.169
I don't want to see him.

18:29.170 --> 18:29.208
Nurse's Office

18:29.580 --> 18:32.170
When I feel this way,

18:32.410 --> 18:34.119
you show up without fail.

18:34.120 --> 18:35.420
Excuse me.

18:36.290 --> 18:37.339
Hori-san.

18:37.340 --> 18:39.120
Eek!

18:40.010 --> 18:41.140
So you did come to school.

18:41.850 --> 18:43.310
Are you feeling sick?

18:44.650 --> 18:47.000
Be quiet and sit still.

18:48.530 --> 18:50.309
Are you dumb or something?

18:50.310 --> 18:52.270
Getting hit in the face
with a ball at your age.

18:53.120 --> 18:55.530
I bet you were spacing out as usual.

18:56.970 --> 18:59.630
Ishikawa-kun's pass was too fast.

19:01.950 --> 19:03.309
It's your fault, Hori-san!

19:03.310 --> 19:03.980
Wha...?!

19:03.981 --> 19:05.901
It's because you said
something weird like that!

19:13.750 --> 19:15.199
Kill me already!

19:15.200 --> 19:16.760
Is this a life-or-death issue?

19:17.290 --> 19:18.519
I won't say it!

19:18.520 --> 19:20.419
I won't say weird things anymore!

19:20.420 --> 19:21.439
Die!

19:21.440 --> 19:22.510
Hori-san!

19:28.150 --> 19:29.970
I shouldn't have said it.

19:30.480 --> 19:32.090
I shouldn't have said it!

19:33.520 --> 19:37.200
But... Miyamura said he loves me too.

19:37.750 --> 19:41.550
No, I bet he was talking
about my hands. No...

19:43.580 --> 19:46.530
I've been thinking about
the same thing since then.

19:46.920 --> 19:48.040
Wow!

19:49.180 --> 19:51.810
I wonder if Miyamura feels the same.

20:10.200 --> 20:11.180
I'm sorry.

20:11.180 --> 20:12.180
Huh?

20:12.580 --> 20:14.530
I didn't bring any cake over today.

20:17.060 --> 20:19.690
You don't have to bring some every time.

20:20.280 --> 20:21.550
Thanks for having me over.

20:23.590 --> 20:25.870
You wrote the wrong kanji!

20:26.300 --> 20:29.240
Why can you write out
"rose" but not "camellia"?

20:29.820 --> 20:32.770
Because I like the shape
of the kanji for rose better.

20:33.140 --> 20:34.370
What's up with that?

20:35.770 --> 20:37.019
I'm glad.

20:37.020 --> 20:39.609
I can talk to him so
casually. Yeah, casually...

20:39.610 --> 20:40.699
Hori-san?

20:40.700 --> 20:42.880
Huh? Wh-What?

20:43.230 --> 20:46.879
I was thinking of making
fruit tarts next time.

20:46.880 --> 20:50.659
Is it OK if I use strawberries?
I won't use blueberries.

20:50.660 --> 20:52.890
Oh, yeah, that's fine.

20:53.450 --> 20:57.530
But you know, it seems like
it's not bothering him at all.

21:02.860 --> 21:04.950
Well, see ya tomorrow.

21:05.200 --> 21:07.140
OK. I'll see you at school.

21:12.320 --> 21:14.250
I wonder if he's forgotten about it.

21:14.630 --> 21:19.290
No, if it's not bothering
him, it's OK, I guess.

21:24.250 --> 21:28.480
How can Hori-san remain so calm like that?

21:30.010 --> 21:31.010
I'm the only one...

21:31.360 --> 21:32.600
I'm the only one...

21:33.210 --> 21:34.650
who's acting like an idiot.

21:46.720 --> 21:53.410
I wonder how far I'll go

21:50.580 --> 21:53.560
Translator tenkenX6

21:54.830 --> 22:01.220
I sigh all alone

22:02.940 --> 22:10.090
I wonder how far I've come

22:10.600 --> 22:13.580
Mamo-chan Eternal_Blizzard

22:11.050 --> 22:17.240
At times I look back

22:13.581 --> 22:16.560
Timers

22:15.640 --> 22:18.605
Eternal_Blizzard

22:17.680 --> 22:25.680
As though I hear faint laughter

22:18.606 --> 22:21.570
Edit, Typeset, and Encode

22:23.591 --> 22:26.570
Quality Check L-E QC Team

22:26.360 --> 22:29.780
Although you were frightened and weak

22:30.400 --> 22:34.959
You tried to find those simple words

22:30.620 --> 22:33.600
Special Thanks

22:33.601 --> 22:36.580
Professor Goomba Suzaku

22:34.960 --> 22:42.559
As we walk hand in hand

22:42.560 --> 22:50.500
I'm sure we'll find our place

22:51.280 --> 22:58.939
in this strange world

22:58.940 --> 23:06.940
with the hope that
tomorrow will always come
